Third-party portions listed in the upstream NOTICE
==================================================

Upstream's NOTICE lists three third-party MIT projects:
  - fazlerocks/jevmail (the lane descriptions, urgency rubric, question instructions and
    0.15 low-confidence threshold in jevkit/mailbox.py)
  - savka777/jev-use (the plan-once design in jevkit/plan.py)
  - rohanarun/computer-use-cache (two cache ideas in jevkit/memo.py and jevkit/plan.py)

None of their text or code is copied into this repository. The computer-use features that
draw on jev-use and computer-use-cache were not ported. jev-mailbox-sort names the five
mailbox lanes (needs_reply, updates, promotional, sales, spam) that the upstream CLI
classifies into; the lane descriptions themselves are not reproduced. Because the lane
design comes from jevmail, its notice is carried here as a precaution:

